# Cloudflare Pages redirects for interlock.sourceshift.ai.
#
# The manual is built under /docs/ -- see site_url and site_dir in
# zensical.toml. Pages reads a _redirects file only from the root of the
# deployed directory, so this one cannot live under docs/ (the build would
# copy it to /docs/_redirects, where it does nothing). The docs workflow
# copies it to site/_redirects before deploying.
#
# Rules match top to bottom and the first match wins. Pages follows a
# matching redirect even when a file exists at the source path, which is why
# there is deliberately no catch-all `/* /docs/:splat`: it would match
# /docs/... itself and loop. Every source below is a path the site served at
# the host root before the move, and nothing else. The list is frozen: a page
# added after the move never lived at the root, so it needs no entry here.
#
# Static rules first, then splat rules, as Pages requires.

# The host root. 302 rather than 301 on purpose: browsers cache a 301 for as
# long as they like, and the root may one day serve something other than a
# pointer at the manual. Everything else below is a permanent move.
/ /docs/ 302

/overview /docs/overview/ 301
/overview/ /docs/overview/ 301
/getting-started /docs/getting-started/ 301
/getting-started/ /docs/getting-started/ 301
/concepts /docs/concepts/ 301
/concepts/ /docs/concepts/ 301
/security-model /docs/security-model/ 301
/security-model/ /docs/security-model/ 301
/sitemap.xml /docs/sitemap.xml 301

/guides/* /docs/guides/:splat 301
/reference/* /docs/reference/:splat 301
/epics/* /docs/epics/:splat 301
/assets/* /docs/assets/:splat 301
